WEBVTT

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:06.329
First Officer's Log,
Stardate 50614.2.

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:09.308
Ensign Kaplan and I
are returning to Voyager

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:12.641
after completing a scouting
mission in the Nekrit Expanse.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.738
The nebula's
completely scrambling

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.305
our navigational readings.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.943
I still can't get a fix
on our position.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:21.647
Are you saying we're lost,
Ensign?

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:24.452
That... depends what
you mean by "lost," sir.

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:25.924
Lost...

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.826
as in you still can't get
a fix on our position.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.490
I'm sorry, sir.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:34.625
Try hailing Voyager again.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.693
No response. We must
still be out of com range.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.671
Then we'll just have to navigate

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:42.004
the old-fashioned way...
engage optical scanners.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.441
Aye, sir.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:52.345
I'm picking up an asteroid field
at coordinates 113 mark 7.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.148
Record it.

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.552
Uh, sir?

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.021
That asteroid field?

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:01.857
It's the same one
we passed two hours ago.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.829
Great.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.491
We're not only lost,
we're flying in circles.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.225
It's a Federation
hailing beacon...

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.137
originating bearing 309 mark 4.

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.731
It's Voyager.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:15.968
Well...

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.738
at least someone knows
where we are.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.211
Setting a course.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.413
The signal's coming
from the planet's surface.

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:30.184
Is it possible Voyager's landed?

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.781
Sensor readings are sketchy.

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:34.794
I'm detecting
about 80,000 humanoid life signs

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.420
on the western continent,

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:38.897
some rudimentary structures
and technology,

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:42.026
but no energy signature
big enough to be a starship.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.770
I'm getting another hail.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.601
The signal's very weak...

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.665
and it's definitely not
being sent by Voyager.

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.768
Try adjusting the bandwidth.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.779
...Colony to Federation vessel.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.474
We need your help, urgently.

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.676
This is Commander Chakotay
of the Starship Voyager.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.412
Please identify yourself.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.783
I'm not reading you.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:03.050
Federation vessel,
please respond to this...

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.852
We lost them, sir.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.950
They've identified us
as a Federation ship.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.426
Who would know that?

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.258
Whoever they are, they're
asking for our help.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.491
Launch a message buoy
letting Voyager know

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.864
we've landed in response
to a distress call.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:27.607
This place looks
like a war zone.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:33.544
I can't pinpoint
the source of the transmission.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.990
Commander.

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:33.660
I'm Commander Chakotay
of the Starship Voyager.

00:04:33.705 --> 00:04:36.105
We're responding
to a distress call.

00:04:36.141 --> 00:04:38.575
We're looking
for whoever it was

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:39.941
that asked for our help.

00:04:39.978 --> 00:04:41.843
Commander!

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:28.254
Come on!

00:05:30.095 --> 00:05:32.086
Take him inside.

00:05:48.313 --> 00:05:51.339
I'd lie still if I were you.

00:05:51.383 --> 00:05:53.715
You've got a nasty head injury.

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:56.152
You're human.

00:05:56.188 --> 00:05:58.315
My name's Riley Frazier.

00:05:58.357 --> 00:05:59.949
What's yours, Commander?

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:01.254
Why did you attack us?

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:03.921
Those weren't my people.

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:06.361
I'm the one
who sent the distress call.

00:06:06.398 --> 00:06:07.592
We rescued you.

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:09.692
What did you do with Kaplan?

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:11.362
Your Ensign.

00:06:11.403 --> 00:06:13.462
She didn't make it.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.232
I'm sorry.

00:06:19.311 --> 00:06:20.903
I've got to get
back to my shuttle.

00:06:20.946 --> 00:06:24.905
Your shuttle isn't there
anymore.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:28.442
The people who attacked you
have already pulled it apart.

00:06:29.621 --> 00:06:31.612
Relax, Commander.

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.818
I'm here to help you.

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:36.718
How did?

00:06:36.762 --> 00:06:38.627
How did I get here?

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:41.189
I could ask you
the same question.

00:06:41.233 --> 00:06:42.598
I was pretty surprised

00:06:42.634 --> 00:06:45.603
when I picked up
a Federation ship out there...

00:06:45.637 --> 00:06:47.662
not that I wasn't happy
about it.

00:06:47.706 --> 00:06:49.469
It's a long story.

00:06:49.508 --> 00:06:51.738
Why don't you go first?

00:06:53.812 --> 00:06:55.609
Seven or eight years ago...

00:06:55.647 --> 00:06:57.376
I was working
as a Science Officer

00:06:57.416 --> 00:06:58.849
on a vessel
in the Bolian sector.

00:06:58.884 --> 00:07:01.512
We were attacked without warning
by aliens.

00:07:01.553 --> 00:07:05.250
They overpowered us in minutes,
and those of us who survived

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:07.781
were put in some kind
of stasis.

00:07:07.826 --> 00:07:11.318
The next thing we knew,
we were here on this planet.

00:07:11.363 --> 00:07:13.695
It didn't take too many hours
of stargazing

00:07:13.732 --> 00:07:16.360
to realize we weren't in
the Alpha Quadrant any longer.

00:07:16.401 --> 00:07:18.164
There are other humans here?

00:07:18.203 --> 00:07:20.034
Three that I know of
besides me...

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.903
what was left of my crew...

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:26.206
along with some Klingons,
Cardassians, Romulans,

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:28.611
and dozens of other species
I'd never seen before.

00:07:28.647 --> 00:07:30.478
And the ones
that put you in stasis?

00:07:30.515 --> 00:07:32.449
I don't know.

00:07:32.484 --> 00:07:35.942
They must have had some kind
of colony here at some time

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:38.718
because of the ruined buildings
and equipment

00:07:38.757 --> 00:07:40.725
they left scattered around.

00:07:40.759 --> 00:07:42.659
We've never seen them again.

00:07:42.694 --> 00:07:45.527
Everyone here has pretty much
the same story.

00:07:45.564 --> 00:07:48.658
They were just grabbed from
wherever they happened to be

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:49.962
and dumped.

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:52.266
Why did those people
kill Kaplan?

00:07:52.304 --> 00:07:54.670
We were no threat to them.

00:07:54.706 --> 00:07:56.970
There are dozens of different
races on this planet,

00:07:57.009 --> 00:07:59.204
all of whom were brought here
against their will.

00:07:59.244 --> 00:08:02.304
Many of them are suspicious
of other species.

00:08:02.347 --> 00:08:05.908
It's not exactly a United
Federation around here,

00:08:05.951 --> 00:08:07.145
if you know what I mean.

00:08:07.185 --> 00:08:10.643
So those kind of attacks...
they go on all the time.

00:08:10.689 --> 00:08:13.214
Resources are pretty limited.

00:08:13.258 --> 00:08:15.749
It didn't take long
for the fighting to start.

00:08:15.794 --> 00:08:17.193
First...

00:08:17.229 --> 00:08:19.663
a group of Klingons
attacked the Cardassians.

00:08:19.698 --> 00:08:21.928
Then the Farn raided the Parein;

00:08:21.967 --> 00:08:24.561
eventually things
just got out of hand,

00:08:24.603 --> 00:08:25.934
and now it's anarchy.

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:28.404
But some of us,
a few hundred or so,

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.738
we've tried to make
the best of it.

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:32.368
We've established
a cooperative...

00:08:32.411 --> 00:08:35.403
sharing work and whatever
provisions we have.

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:39.384
I've got to contact my ship.

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:42.751
The raiders destroyed
the communications array.

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:44.949
It'll take days to fix it.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.480
I can help you.

00:08:50.028 --> 00:08:52.053
Our medic examined you.

00:08:52.097 --> 00:08:53.962
You suffered serious
neural trauma.

00:08:53.999 --> 00:08:55.398
You're staying put.

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:58.494
And that's an order, Commander.

00:09:03.308 --> 00:09:07.369
Captain's Log, Stardate 50622.4.

00:09:07.412 --> 00:09:08.674
While Commander Chakotay

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:11.012
scouts for a faster route
through the Nekrit Expanse,

00:09:11.049 --> 00:09:13.244
we are continuing
our month-long journey

00:09:13.285 --> 00:09:15.651
through the sparsely
populated region.

00:09:15.687 --> 00:09:16.915
You know, they ought to rename

00:09:16.955 --> 00:09:19.185
this place
the "negative expanse."

00:09:19.224 --> 00:09:22.022
We haven't run across
anything interesting for days.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:23.391
If you're bored, Mr. Paris,

00:09:23.428 --> 00:09:25.828
I'm sure I can find
something else for you to do.

00:09:25.864 --> 00:09:29.322
The warp plasma filters are due
for a thorough cleaning.

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:31.928
Now that you mention it,
Captain,

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:36.737
I find this region of space
a real navigational challenge.

00:09:37.776 --> 00:09:39.573
I believe I may have found
something else

00:09:39.611 --> 00:09:41.340
to pique
Mr. Paris's interest, Captain.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:43.814
It's an unidentified ship
on long-range sensors.

00:09:43.849 --> 00:09:45.316
What sort of ship?

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:46.908
Sensor readings
are very limited,

00:09:46.952 --> 00:09:48.419
but the vessel
appears to be stopped

00:09:48.453 --> 00:09:50.284
directly in our current
flight path.

00:09:50.322 --> 00:09:51.949
Harry, send
a standard greeting.

00:09:52.023 --> 00:09:53.251
Aye, Captain.

00:09:54.726 --> 00:09:55.954
They're not responding.

00:09:55.994 --> 00:09:58.861
Try retransmitting the hail
on wide-band subspace.

00:09:58.897 --> 00:10:00.592
Still no response.

00:10:00.632 --> 00:10:01.963
We are entering visual range.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.433
On screen.

00:10:05.837 --> 00:10:07.168
The Borg.

00:10:07.205 --> 00:10:08.934
Red Alert.

00:10:16.148 --> 00:10:17.342
All stop.
Shields to maximum.

00:10:17.382 --> 00:10:18.576
Stand by all weapons.

00:10:18.617 --> 00:10:20.244
Tuvok, are they scanning us?

00:10:20.285 --> 00:10:21.309
Curious.

00:10:21.353 --> 00:10:24.379
None of the Borg systems
appears to be operational.

00:10:24.423 --> 00:10:26.391
He's right.
They're adrift.

00:10:26.425 --> 00:10:29.690
Maybe they're trying to lull us
into a false sense of security.

00:10:29.728 --> 00:10:32.390
That would not be consistent
with typical Borg tactics.

00:10:32.431 --> 00:10:34.160
I want to try
a multiphasic scan.

00:10:34.199 --> 00:10:36.360
Tom, stand by to get us
out of here in case they react.

00:10:36.401 --> 00:10:37.425
Aye, Captain.

00:10:37.469 --> 00:10:39.630
Proceed, Mr. Kim.

00:10:39.671 --> 00:10:42.640
I'm not picking up
any active energy signatures.

00:10:42.674 --> 00:10:44.972
And no life signs.

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:45.999
Well, that's a relief.

00:10:46.077 --> 00:10:47.101
Perhaps.

00:10:47.145 --> 00:10:49.306
However, we should avoid
complacency.

00:10:49.347 --> 00:10:51.144
The Borg are known to retrieve

00:10:51.183 --> 00:10:52.548
their damaged technology.

00:10:52.584 --> 00:10:53.642
It is quite possible

00:10:53.685 --> 00:10:55.380
we will encounter
additional Borg vessels

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:57.581
which are fully manned
and powered.

00:10:57.622 --> 00:11:00.591
That's exactly why we're going
to board that ship.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:02.757
Captain?

00:11:02.794 --> 00:11:03.920
This is a rare opportunity

00:11:03.962 --> 00:11:06.123
to learn as much as we can
about Borg technology.

00:11:06.164 --> 00:11:09.156
I might be able to get
one of their data nodes running

00:11:09.201 --> 00:11:10.759
and find out
what disabled their ship.

00:11:10.802 --> 00:11:11.860
If we're lucky,

00:11:11.903 --> 00:11:14.463
we may find a weakness
we can use against them,

00:11:14.506 --> 00:11:15.632
in case we run into one

00:11:15.674 --> 00:11:17.665
of their fully manned
and powered ships.

00:11:17.709 --> 00:11:18.903
Tuvok, assemble an away team.

00:11:18.944 --> 00:11:19.911
Tom...

00:11:19.945 --> 00:11:21.936
Yes, Captain.

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:24.505
...take us
into transporter range.

00:11:27.986 --> 00:11:30.614
We grow all our own food
in a cooperative garden.

00:11:30.655 --> 00:11:31.644
It's delicious.

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:32.987
Sorry there's no meat.

00:11:33.024 --> 00:11:34.082
No problem.

00:11:34.125 --> 00:11:35.149
I'm a vegetarian.

00:11:35.193 --> 00:11:36.490
Really?

00:11:36.528 --> 00:11:38.519
I have recurring dreams

00:11:38.563 --> 00:11:41.999
about my mother's
famous Texas barbecue.

00:11:42.033 --> 00:11:43.830
So, your journey home...

00:11:43.869 --> 00:11:47.168
how much longer do you
expect it'll take you?

00:11:47.205 --> 00:11:48.672
About 67 years.

00:11:48.707 --> 00:11:52.666
Provided we don't find
a wormhole

00:11:52.711 --> 00:11:55.544
or some other faster way
of getting back.

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:58.981
Haven't you ever thought about
finding some nice M-Class planet

00:11:59.017 --> 00:12:00.348
and putting down roots?

00:12:00.385 --> 00:12:02.649
We'd be missing
an incredible opportunity

00:12:02.687 --> 00:12:04.120
to explore unknown space.

00:12:04.155 --> 00:12:07.249
Besides, we've made a good life
for ourselves on Voyager.

00:12:07.292 --> 00:12:09.590
I'm sure Captain Janeway
would be amenable

00:12:09.628 --> 00:12:12.961
to take as many of your people
with us as we can accommodate.

00:12:13.031 --> 00:12:14.396
Take us with you?

00:12:14.432 --> 00:12:16.866
I assumed that's why
you sent the distress call.

00:12:16.902 --> 00:12:18.494
You misunderstood.

00:12:18.537 --> 00:12:19.970
We want to stay.

00:12:20.038 --> 00:12:22.370
But you were brought here
against your will.

00:12:22.407 --> 00:12:24.238
You just said
how dangerous it is.

00:12:24.276 --> 00:12:27.712
For better or worse,
this place has become our home.

00:12:27.746 --> 00:12:29.976
The people
in the cooperative...

00:12:30.015 --> 00:12:31.676
they're like my ancestors...

00:12:31.716 --> 00:12:32.774
Texas homesteaders.

00:12:32.817 --> 00:12:34.307
I can understand that, but...

00:12:34.352 --> 00:12:35.717
We have a deep connection

00:12:35.754 --> 00:12:38.314
to one another
that I've never felt before,

00:12:38.356 --> 00:12:40.881
not even with members
of my own family.

00:12:40.926 --> 00:12:44.259
I guess it's because of what
we've all gone through together.

00:12:44.296 --> 00:12:46.787
What about those unfriendly
neighbors of yours?

00:12:46.831 --> 00:12:49.732
We've been able to bring
a few of them into our group.

00:12:49.768 --> 00:12:52.601
But you're right,
they're a problem.

00:12:54.139 --> 00:12:56.266
That's why we want your help.

00:12:56.308 --> 00:12:58.242
Security upgrades,

00:12:58.276 --> 00:13:00.938
medical supplies,
maybe some weapons.

00:13:00.979 --> 00:13:03.504
We're creating a society here...

00:13:03.548 --> 00:13:06.449
one that's based on tolerance,
shared responsibility,

00:13:06.484 --> 00:13:09.044
and mutual respect...
that people like you and I

00:13:09.087 --> 00:13:10.611
were raised to believe in.

00:13:10.655 --> 00:13:14.022
We're not about to give it up
just because it's difficult.

00:13:15.827 --> 00:13:19.422
I'd better get back to work
on the communications array.

00:13:19.464 --> 00:13:20.260
I'll come with you.

00:13:20.298 --> 00:13:21.424
No!

00:13:22.734 --> 00:13:27.103
You're still in no shape
to fight, if we're attacked.

00:13:29.274 --> 00:13:32.266
I'll be back
to check on you soon.

00:14:00.639 --> 00:14:03.107
It's like a ghost ship.

00:14:03.141 --> 00:14:05.803
Allowing yourself
to become apprehensive

00:14:05.844 --> 00:14:08.312
can only be counterproductive,
Lieutenant.

00:14:08.346 --> 00:14:10.780
I'm not being apprehensive,
Tuvok.

00:14:10.815 --> 00:14:12.806
I'm just nervous as hell.

00:14:31.503 --> 00:14:32.970
This is one of the access nodes.

00:14:33.004 --> 00:14:34.972
If we can get it operational,

00:14:35.006 --> 00:14:39.636
I should be able to tap
into the main data systems.

00:14:39.678 --> 00:14:41.578
Tuvok...

00:14:41.613 --> 00:14:44.639
there should be a compatible
micro-power conduit

00:14:44.683 --> 00:14:46.241
somewhere in that module.

00:14:46.284 --> 00:14:48.548
Connect it to this generator.

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:07.871
Lieutenant.

00:15:12.976 --> 00:15:14.671
It's dead.

00:15:16.746 --> 00:15:17.940
As far as we can tell,

00:15:17.981 --> 00:15:21.280
all activity on the Borg ship
ceased abruptly five years ago.

00:15:21.317 --> 00:15:24.548
Our scans have detected
1,100 corpses.

00:15:24.587 --> 00:15:26.851
We located a breached
section of the vessel

00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:28.448
where the spatial
vacuum preserved

00:15:28.491 --> 00:15:29.958
several of the bodies perfectly.

00:15:30.026 --> 00:15:31.288
We brought one aboard.

00:15:31.327 --> 00:15:32.351
We're hoping that an autopsy

00:15:32.395 --> 00:15:33.953
might give us some clue
as to what killed them.

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.156
The question is:

00:15:35.198 --> 00:15:37.723
Why have the Borg
left one of their ships

00:15:37.767 --> 00:15:41.601
and all its technology adrift
in space for anyone to find?

00:15:41.638 --> 00:15:43.868
It is possible that
the deactivation of the ship

00:15:43.907 --> 00:15:45.499
and its systems

00:15:45.541 --> 00:15:47.372
severed the link
with the rest of the collective.

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:49.435
But what caused the shutdown
in the first place?

00:15:49.479 --> 00:15:51.970
It could've been some kind
of natural disaster...

00:15:52.081 --> 00:15:54.379
or...

00:15:54.417 --> 00:15:55.850
Or what?

00:15:57.453 --> 00:16:00.684
Maybe the Borg were defeated
by an enemy

00:16:00.723 --> 00:16:03.521
even more powerful
than they were.

00:16:05.228 --> 00:16:08.197
Tuvok, continue scanning
for any Borg vessels

00:16:08.231 --> 00:16:09.562
in the vicinity,

00:16:09.599 --> 00:16:12.932
as well as any other ships
that might be more powerful.

00:16:12.969 --> 00:16:16.063
B'Elanna, you and the Doctor
get started on that autopsy.

00:16:16.105 --> 00:16:18.869
In the meantime,
I think it would be a good idea

00:16:18.908 --> 00:16:20.933
to rendezvous
with Commander Chakotay

00:16:20.977 --> 00:16:22.444
a little ahead of schedule,

00:16:22.478 --> 00:16:26.107
and let him know we've
run into some old friends.

00:17:02.618 --> 00:17:04.609
Hello? Anybody there?

00:17:08.958 --> 00:17:10.949
Riley?

00:18:20.229 --> 00:18:21.924
Riley?

00:18:30.506 --> 00:18:31.837
What are you?

00:18:31.874 --> 00:18:33.603
Are you Borg?

00:18:33.643 --> 00:18:35.804
We were Borg.

00:18:35.845 --> 00:18:37.870
You mean you weren't
just kidnapped,

00:18:37.914 --> 00:18:40.144
you were assimilated
by the collective.

00:18:40.183 --> 00:18:42.151
At Wolf 359.

00:18:42.185 --> 00:18:44.380
I was a Science Officer
aboard the Roosevelt.

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:45.751
But five years ago,

00:18:45.788 --> 00:18:48.279
our cube was damaged
by an electrokinetic storm.

00:18:48.324 --> 00:18:49.621
The next thing we knew,

00:18:49.659 --> 00:18:51.251
our link to the collective
was severed.

00:18:51.294 --> 00:18:52.784
We were free.

00:18:52.829 --> 00:18:54.319
We could think
for ourselves again,

00:18:54.363 --> 00:18:55.330
remember our names,

00:18:55.364 --> 00:18:56.592
where we'd come from.

00:18:56.632 --> 00:18:58.429
It was like waking up
from a long nightmare.

00:18:58.468 --> 00:18:59.696
We took what we
thought we could use,

00:18:59.735 --> 00:19:01.430
and transported ourselves here.

00:19:01.471 --> 00:19:04.338
Everything was new again...
the sounds of our own voices,

00:19:04.373 --> 00:19:06.898
forgotten memories,
the taste of food.

00:19:06.976 --> 00:19:09.410
Our original skin pigmentation
began to come back.

00:19:09.445 --> 00:19:11.913
Many of us were able to remove
our Borg appendages.

00:19:12.014 --> 00:19:13.242
I was even lucky enough

00:19:13.282 --> 00:19:15.307
to get a prosthetic arm
Orum created,

00:19:15.351 --> 00:19:17.012
using Borg replication
equipment.

00:19:17.053 --> 00:19:20.181
In spite of how little we had,
it was a joyous, hopeful time.

00:19:20.223 --> 00:19:21.485
And then?

00:19:21.524 --> 00:19:23.822
After the euphoria wore off,

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:25.725
people started looking around,

00:19:25.761 --> 00:19:27.729
and found they were living
among other cultures

00:19:27.763 --> 00:19:28.752
they didn't understand...

00:19:28.798 --> 00:19:32.063
or worse, species
they'd been taught to hate.

00:19:32.101 --> 00:19:33.398
They turned against one another.

00:19:33.436 --> 00:19:34.835
Things became chaotic.

00:19:34.871 --> 00:19:36.361
The fighting, the raids...

00:19:36.405 --> 00:19:37.929
But we're not all like that.

00:19:37.974 --> 00:19:40.033
Everything I told you
about forming a cooperative,

00:19:40.076 --> 00:19:41.839
building a new society...
I meant it.

00:19:41.878 --> 00:19:44.870
Riley's telling the truth,
Commander Chakotay.

00:19:44.914 --> 00:19:46.711
Look at me... I was Romulan.

00:19:46.749 --> 00:19:49.115
I was taught to hate
humans, the Federation...

00:19:49.152 --> 00:19:50.779
but Riley and I are friends now.

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:51.946
I'm part of the cooperative.

00:19:52.054 --> 00:19:52.952
Orum's our medic.

00:19:53.055 --> 00:19:54.147
He's the one who examined you.

00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:56.681
Why didn't you tell me all this
in the first place?

00:19:56.726 --> 00:19:59.752
I know how people feel
about the Borg,

00:19:59.795 --> 00:20:01.262
and they're right.

00:20:01.297 --> 00:20:03.162
We did terrible things.

00:20:03.199 --> 00:20:04.393
You'd been assimilated.

00:20:04.433 --> 00:20:06.458
You weren't in control
of your actions.

00:20:06.502 --> 00:20:08.663
Then you'll still help us?

00:20:12.275 --> 00:20:13.640
I think, right now,

00:20:13.676 --> 00:20:16.702
it's Commander Chakotay
who needs our help.

00:20:16.746 --> 00:20:19.078
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:20:19.115 --> 00:20:20.810
We've detected a message buoy

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:22.784
launched
from Chakotay's shuttle

00:20:22.818 --> 00:20:24.479
and are heading toward it.

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:27.011
The autopsy of the Borg corpse
is underway.

00:20:31.427 --> 00:20:34.396
I must say, there's nothing
like the vacuum of space

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:36.830
for preserving
a handsome corpse.

00:20:41.037 --> 00:20:42.834
Hmm...

00:20:42.872 --> 00:20:45.807
Subject's abdominal organs
are unremarkable.

00:20:45.841 --> 00:20:47.900
Pulmonary system
exhibits evidence

00:20:47.944 --> 00:20:51.311
of extensive alveolar damage,
as well as a slight swelling

00:20:51.347 --> 00:20:53.679
consistent
with exposure to space...

00:20:53.716 --> 00:20:54.944
Ah...

00:20:54.984 --> 00:20:57.009
In addition, there are signs

00:20:57.086 --> 00:20:59.452
of severe cardiac
depolarization.

00:20:59.488 --> 00:21:01.353
It sounds like
he was electrocuted.

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:02.357
Very good, Kes.

00:21:02.391 --> 00:21:03.824
That would support our theory

00:21:03.859 --> 00:21:05.724
about what happened
aboard their ship.

00:21:05.761 --> 00:21:08.252
We think that their main power
conduits were overloaded

00:21:08.297 --> 00:21:10.356
by a massive
electro-mechanical discharge.

00:21:10.399 --> 00:21:11.366
Hmm...

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:13.698
This is intriguing.

00:21:13.736 --> 00:21:15.636
What do you think that is?

00:21:15.671 --> 00:21:18.196
It may be some sort
of axonal amplifier.

00:21:18.241 --> 00:21:20.038
Kes, hand me a cortical probe.

00:21:33.689 --> 00:21:34.986
Shut it down!

00:21:45.201 --> 00:21:47.431
What the hell happened?

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:48.732
Is it still alive?

00:21:48.771 --> 00:21:50.295
Of course not.

00:21:50.339 --> 00:21:53.001
Apparently,
I inadvertently activated

00:21:53.075 --> 00:21:56.909
a backup neuroelectric
power cell.

00:21:56.946 --> 00:21:58.413
The response
was purely autonomic.

00:21:58.447 --> 00:22:00.506
There's no reason for concern.

00:22:00.549 --> 00:22:02.346
I wouldn't be so sure
about that.

00:22:02.385 --> 00:22:03.647
What do you mean?

00:22:03.686 --> 00:22:05.950
That "autonomic response"
caused this drone

00:22:05.988 --> 00:22:09.219
to reset back
to its original programming.

00:22:09.258 --> 00:22:12.819
If the rest of those corpses
somehow reactivate...

00:22:12.862 --> 00:22:15.797
we'd have a major problem
on our hands.

00:22:21.604 --> 00:22:23.231
I'm afraid he's getting worse.

00:22:23.272 --> 00:22:25.638
There must be something
we can do for him.

00:22:25.675 --> 00:22:27.165
You know better than anyone

00:22:27.209 --> 00:22:29.336
how limited our
medical resources are.

00:22:29.378 --> 00:22:32.711
As far as I'm concerned,
there is only one option.

00:22:32.748 --> 00:22:34.682
Would it be safe?

00:22:35.785 --> 00:22:38.345
Would... what be safe?

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:42.623
As I'm sure you're aware,

00:22:42.658 --> 00:22:44.626
the Borg collective
consciousness

00:22:44.660 --> 00:22:46.184
is extremely powerful.

00:22:46.228 --> 00:22:49.288
It allowed us to transfer
information instantaneously...

00:22:49.332 --> 00:22:50.731
to think with one mind.

00:22:50.766 --> 00:22:53.360
But what you may not be aware of

00:22:53.402 --> 00:22:57.395
is the link also has
inherent medical applications.

00:22:57.440 --> 00:23:00.705
M-m-medical applications?

00:23:00.743 --> 00:23:02.870
We were connected
by a continuous

00:23:02.912 --> 00:23:06.439
neuroelectric field
that was capable of regenerating

00:23:06.482 --> 00:23:09.144
the damaged components
of an injured Borg.

00:23:09.185 --> 00:23:11.483
Think of it
as a subspace transfusion.

00:23:11.520 --> 00:23:13.886
Only instead of one person
giving blood,

00:23:13.923 --> 00:23:16.949
there are hundreds,
perhaps thousands, of donors

00:23:17.026 --> 00:23:19.256
simultaneously transmitting
neuroelectric energy

00:23:19.295 --> 00:23:20.819
to whoever needed it.

00:23:20.863 --> 00:23:23.559
This process
was often successful

00:23:23.599 --> 00:23:26.762
in healing both organic
and inorganic body parts.

00:23:26.802 --> 00:23:29.566
This is all... very fascinating,

00:23:29.605 --> 00:23:32.438
but I don't see how it helps me.

00:23:32.475 --> 00:23:34.875
We still have Borg
neural processors implanted

00:23:34.910 --> 00:23:36.377
in our nervous systems.

00:23:36.412 --> 00:23:38.380
Removing them
would've killed us.

00:23:38.414 --> 00:23:40.245
I see.

00:23:40.282 --> 00:23:42.341
Using a portable
neuro-transponder,

00:23:42.385 --> 00:23:45.445
we have the ability
to relink our brain patterns.

00:23:45.488 --> 00:23:47.353
I thought you said
the link was severed.

00:23:47.390 --> 00:23:48.618
It was.

00:23:48.657 --> 00:23:50.352
But we can reinitiate it

00:23:50.393 --> 00:23:52.452
among a small group,
for a short time.

00:23:52.495 --> 00:23:54.895
We could generate
a neuroelectric field

00:23:54.930 --> 00:23:56.795
that could heal your injuries.

00:23:56.832 --> 00:24:01.701
You want to... hook up my mind
to some... Borg collective?

00:24:01.737 --> 00:24:03.398
No, no, that's not it at all.

00:24:03.439 --> 00:24:05.236
We'd be in complete control.

00:24:05.274 --> 00:24:07.936
You'd simply be linked,
for a limited period of time,

00:24:08.010 --> 00:24:10.808
to Riley, me, and a few
of the others in our group

00:24:10.846 --> 00:24:12.370
willing to help you.

00:24:12.415 --> 00:24:14.508
I'm not letting anyone implant

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:16.814
some neural processor
in my brain.

00:24:16.852 --> 00:24:18.342
That wouldn't be necessary.

00:24:18.387 --> 00:24:20.480
I'd simply attach
a small neuro-transceiver

00:24:20.523 --> 00:24:22.115
to the base of your skull.

00:24:22.158 --> 00:24:23.955
We'd initiate the link,
and the transceiver

00:24:24.059 --> 00:24:26.823
could be removed as soon
as the procedure was over.

00:24:26.862 --> 00:24:29.490
I assure you, other than
repairing neural tissue,

00:24:29.532 --> 00:24:31.557
there would be
no lasting effects.

00:24:31.600 --> 00:24:34.160
Thanks...

00:24:34.203 --> 00:24:35.966
but I don't think so.

00:24:36.005 --> 00:24:39.065
I-I can see
why you're skeptical.

00:24:39.108 --> 00:24:40.735
I would be, too.

00:24:40.776 --> 00:24:43.643
Look around you...
Orum and I, the others...

00:24:43.679 --> 00:24:44.976
we're individuals.

00:24:45.047 --> 00:24:46.947
We have distinct personalities.

00:24:46.982 --> 00:24:51.942
We're not about to turn you
into some kind of automaton.

00:24:51.987 --> 00:24:54.615
I'll take my chances
and wait for Voyager.

00:24:54.657 --> 00:24:58.115
I'm afraid that help
may come too late, Commander.

00:24:58.160 --> 00:24:59.821
If we don't do something

00:24:59.862 --> 00:25:02.922
to slow the neural degradation
immediately...

00:25:02.965 --> 00:25:04.796
you will die.

00:25:13.342 --> 00:25:15.310
Chakotay...

00:25:15.344 --> 00:25:17.676
you have to make a decision.

00:25:19.915 --> 00:25:21.473
Any sign of Voyager?

00:25:21.517 --> 00:25:22.814
No.

00:25:22.852 --> 00:25:24.649
I can't change who we are.

00:25:24.687 --> 00:25:26.951
I wasn't truthful with you
before, and I'm sorry,

00:25:27.022 --> 00:25:28.956
but please, believe me
when I tell you

00:25:29.024 --> 00:25:31.151
we only want to help you.

00:25:31.193 --> 00:25:33.457
Orum will take every precaution.

00:25:33.496 --> 00:25:34.861
Please?

00:25:34.897 --> 00:25:37.491
At least let us
try and save you.

00:25:37.533 --> 00:25:38.898
It's either that

00:25:38.934 --> 00:25:41.368
or the happy hunting grounds,
huh?

00:25:41.403 --> 00:25:44.133
Okay, then?

00:26:00.823 --> 00:26:03.553
This is the neuro-transceiver.

00:26:20.009 --> 00:26:22.273
Don't be afraid, Chakotay.

00:26:22.311 --> 00:26:23.801
We're here to help you.

00:26:23.846 --> 00:26:25.714
Open your mind to our thoughts,

00:26:25.847 --> 00:26:28.645
and concentrate
on getting well.

00:26:28.683 --> 00:26:30.708
Hear our voices.

00:26:30.752 --> 00:26:33.482
Open your mind to our thoughts.

00:26:33.521 --> 00:26:36.285
Our collective strength
can heal you.

00:26:36.324 --> 00:26:38.554
You're safe with us.

00:26:38.593 --> 00:26:39.958
Feel the connection.

00:26:40.061 --> 00:26:41.255
We're with you.

00:26:41.296 --> 00:26:42.729
See who we are.

00:26:42.764 --> 00:26:43.856
Know us.

00:26:43.898 --> 00:26:45.388
You're not alone.

00:26:45.433 --> 00:26:47.924
Our strength is your strength.

00:26:47.969 --> 00:26:50.961
We can overcome your pain.

00:26:51.072 --> 00:26:53.802
We welcome you
into our thoughts.

00:26:53.842 --> 00:26:55.139
There's nothing to fear.

00:26:55.176 --> 00:26:57.303
We won't let you die.

00:26:57.345 --> 00:27:01.577
We're all one circle...
no beginning, no end.

00:27:17.499 --> 00:27:18.488
Grandpa!

00:27:36.851 --> 00:27:38.648
How do you feel?

00:27:39.687 --> 00:27:41.848
Don't worry.
It's gone.

00:27:44.025 --> 00:27:46.289
It looks like
the treatment worked.

00:27:46.327 --> 00:27:51.162
Orum says the degraded tissue
has shown marked improvement.

00:27:53.835 --> 00:27:55.632
It was incredible.

00:27:57.472 --> 00:27:58.837
I know.

00:28:01.810 --> 00:28:07.112
I heard all of you...
your thoughts inside my head...

00:28:07.148 --> 00:28:09.446
as if they were my thoughts.

00:28:09.484 --> 00:28:12.282
And I could see myself...

00:28:12.320 --> 00:28:14.015
through your eyes.

00:28:14.055 --> 00:28:16.455
Then you must have
caught me staring.

00:28:17.926 --> 00:28:19.655
I saw...

00:28:19.694 --> 00:28:22.925
faces... planets...

00:28:22.964 --> 00:28:24.397
What were they?

00:28:24.432 --> 00:28:29.233
Lmages from the minds of
the people who linked with you.

00:28:29.270 --> 00:28:32.239
Members of their families,
their homes...

00:28:32.273 --> 00:28:36.403
I know things
about all of them...

00:28:36.444 --> 00:28:37.968
about you.

00:28:39.480 --> 00:28:41.505
You like bluebonnets.

00:28:41.549 --> 00:28:43.141
My favorite flower.

00:28:43.184 --> 00:28:44.674
You used to pick them

00:28:44.719 --> 00:28:49.315
back home in Texas with a man
who carried a walking stick.

00:28:49.357 --> 00:28:51.484
My grandfather.

00:28:51.526 --> 00:28:53.687
I know so much about you.

00:28:53.728 --> 00:28:57.289
We shared
a very rare experience.

00:29:04.806 --> 00:29:06.831
I felt that.

00:29:10.812 --> 00:29:12.643
What about this?

00:29:16.651 --> 00:29:19.313
It's a residual effect
from the link.

00:29:21.155 --> 00:29:23.521
How long will it last?

00:29:23.558 --> 00:29:25.651
An hour.

00:29:25.693 --> 00:29:27.888
Maybe two.

00:29:27.929 --> 00:29:31.729
Long enough.

00:29:31.766 --> 00:29:33.927
Can you still hear
what I'm thinking?

00:29:34.002 --> 00:29:35.401
Yes.

00:29:35.436 --> 00:29:37.802
Then you know I want to be
closer to you.

00:29:39.741 --> 00:29:44.201
I want us to know
everything about each other.

00:29:44.245 --> 00:29:47.806
I want you to feel
everything I feel.

00:30:04.032 --> 00:30:05.192
According to the buoy,

00:30:05.233 --> 00:30:07.133
Commander Chakotay
and Ensign Kaplan

00:30:07.168 --> 00:30:08.635
landed on the surface
in response

00:30:08.670 --> 00:30:09.796
to a distress call
three days ago.

00:30:09.837 --> 00:30:10.963
Can you locate the shuttle?

00:30:12.073 --> 00:30:14.974
There is no sign of it
anywhere on the planet.

00:30:15.076 --> 00:30:16.976
What about their combadges?

00:30:17.078 --> 00:30:18.705
I'm only picking up one signal.

00:30:18.746 --> 00:30:20.714
It's
in a heavily populated region.

00:30:20.748 --> 00:30:22.375
Signal's very weak.

00:30:22.417 --> 00:30:24.385
Voyager to Commander Chakotay.

00:30:24.419 --> 00:30:26.751
Do you read?

00:30:26.788 --> 00:30:28.449
Ensign Kaplan,
this is Captain Janeway.

00:30:28.489 --> 00:30:29.581
Come in.

00:30:29.624 --> 00:30:31.319
Electrodynamic turbulence
from the nebula

00:30:31.359 --> 00:30:32.917
is interfering
with the transmission.

00:30:32.961 --> 00:30:34.588
It's going to take me
a while to clear it up.

00:30:42.270 --> 00:30:44.261
Hand me that hyper-spanner.

00:30:48.776 --> 00:30:49.743
There.

00:30:49.777 --> 00:30:51.005
That should at least get

00:30:51.112 --> 00:30:53.307
the short-range
transmitters operational.

00:30:53.348 --> 00:30:54.645
Now, if we can get

00:30:54.682 --> 00:30:56.377
the signal amplifiers
on line...

00:30:56.417 --> 00:30:57.850
I never would've figured you

00:30:57.885 --> 00:31:00.012
to be quite so handy
with a circuitry panel.

00:31:00.121 --> 00:31:01.554
Well, I guess
you haven't learned

00:31:01.589 --> 00:31:02.886
everything about me, have you?

00:31:02.924 --> 00:31:07.361
Commander, I just wanted to say
how grateful to you we all are.

00:31:07.395 --> 00:31:09.829
You're the ones
who saved my life.

00:31:09.864 --> 00:31:12.526
But you've added so much
to the cooperative...

00:31:12.567 --> 00:31:15.502
a renewed sense of hope,
an infusion of energy.

00:31:15.536 --> 00:31:17.936
You have no idea
how invigorating it was

00:31:17.972 --> 00:31:19.701
to have a new mind in the link,

00:31:19.741 --> 00:31:21.868
even if it was only
for a short time.

00:31:21.909 --> 00:31:25.709
There have been so few of us
for so long, I...

00:31:25.747 --> 00:31:28.910
Well, I'll let you two
get back to work.

00:31:33.087 --> 00:31:35.681
I was so resistant
to being linked.

00:31:35.723 --> 00:31:38.214
Now I'm almost sorry it's over.

00:31:38.259 --> 00:31:39.453
I know.

00:31:41.629 --> 00:31:43.221
Last night, when we
were still connected,

00:31:43.264 --> 00:31:46.233
I realized what it is
you really want from us.

00:31:46.267 --> 00:31:50.601
It's more than just supplies
and security upgrades.

00:31:50.638 --> 00:31:52.265
That's right.

00:31:52.306 --> 00:31:53.864
It's a pretty radical concept.

00:31:53.908 --> 00:31:57.002
Sometimes radical problems
require radical solutions.

00:31:57.111 --> 00:31:59.204
Riley!
Commander Chakotay!

00:31:59.247 --> 00:32:01.010
We've detected a ship in orbit.

00:32:01.049 --> 00:32:02.346
It must be Voyager.

00:32:02.383 --> 00:32:04.681
I hope you'll at least
discuss our idea

00:32:04.719 --> 00:32:06.687
with your Captain.

00:32:06.721 --> 00:32:09.884
Why don't you tell her
about it yourself?

00:32:14.028 --> 00:32:15.962
We've given it
a great deal of thought,

00:32:16.030 --> 00:32:18.225
and we believe the solution
to our problem

00:32:18.266 --> 00:32:20.200
is to reestablish
the neural link

00:32:20.234 --> 00:32:22.725
among all the former Borg
living on the planet.

00:32:22.770 --> 00:32:24.829
You can't be serious.

00:32:24.872 --> 00:32:26.669
I know it sounds extreme,
Captain,

00:32:26.707 --> 00:32:28.641
but I think you
should hear her out.

00:32:28.676 --> 00:32:31.076
All right.

00:32:31.112 --> 00:32:33.080
If you'll think about it,
Captain,

00:32:33.114 --> 00:32:35.639
when we were linked,
we had no ethnic conflict.

00:32:35.683 --> 00:32:39.380
There was no crime, no hunger,
no health problems.

00:32:39.420 --> 00:32:41.911
We lived
as one harmonious family.

00:32:41.956 --> 00:32:43.924
With all due respect,
Dr. Frazier,

00:32:43.958 --> 00:32:45.983
you were "one harmonious family"

00:32:46.094 --> 00:32:49.530
bent on the violent assimilation
of innocent cultures.

00:32:49.564 --> 00:32:53.330
But we're not Borg anymore,
and we've learned from our past.

00:32:53.367 --> 00:32:56.393
All we want to do
is to take the one good thing

00:32:56.437 --> 00:32:59.429
that existed in the midst
of all that horror...

00:32:59.474 --> 00:33:02.739
our unique ability to cooperate
and problem-solve...

00:33:02.777 --> 00:33:06.304
and use it to create a safe
and productive community.

00:33:06.347 --> 00:33:08.212
Tell me how, exactly.

00:33:09.984 --> 00:33:11.952
The neuro-transponder
we've built

00:33:12.053 --> 00:33:14.954
is only powerful enough
to link a small group of people,

00:33:15.056 --> 00:33:19.117
like the one that helped heal
Chakotay's wounds.

00:33:19.160 --> 00:33:20.855
In any case,
the effect is only temporary.

00:33:20.895 --> 00:33:23.887
In order to reconnect the
entire population permanently,

00:33:23.931 --> 00:33:27.298
we'd need a much bigger
neuroelectric field generator.

00:33:27.335 --> 00:33:29.735
I'm afraid we don't have
anything like that.

00:33:29.770 --> 00:33:31.738
But the Borg cube does.

00:33:31.772 --> 00:33:33.535
What they're asking us to do

00:33:33.574 --> 00:33:36.338
is reactivate that ship's
neuroelectric generator

00:33:36.377 --> 00:33:38.345
and redirect it
toward the planet.

00:33:41.082 --> 00:33:45.746
They want us to reactivate...
a Borg ship?

00:33:45.786 --> 00:33:47.879
Not the whole ship,
just the generator.

00:33:47.922 --> 00:33:50.447
And it only needs to be
operational for a few minutes,

00:33:50.491 --> 00:33:52.186
in order to reactivate
the link.

00:33:52.226 --> 00:33:53.693
There's no telling
what would happen

00:33:53.728 --> 00:33:56.288
if we turned on one of those
generators, even for an instant.

00:33:56.330 --> 00:33:58.560
For all we know, it would
attract other Borg vessels.

00:33:58.599 --> 00:34:02.933
Captain, I can assure you,
we'd take every precaution.

00:34:04.372 --> 00:34:06.932
Dr. Frazier,
I admire your tenacity.

00:34:07.041 --> 00:34:09.703
I respect your courage.

00:34:11.712 --> 00:34:13.737
I'll give you medical supplies.

00:34:13.781 --> 00:34:15.373
I'll assist you
with upgrading your security.

00:34:15.416 --> 00:34:17.680
I'll even take
some of you with us,

00:34:17.718 --> 00:34:18.946
if you want to come.

00:34:19.053 --> 00:34:21.180
But as to what you're proposing,

00:34:21.222 --> 00:34:23.952
I have to tell you,
I'm extremely skeptical.

00:34:24.058 --> 00:34:26.959
In fairness, however,

00:34:26.994 --> 00:34:29.189
I will give it
some further thought.

00:34:29.230 --> 00:34:30.561
Thank you.

00:34:40.174 --> 00:34:41.607
What do you think?

00:34:41.642 --> 00:34:44.873
If you're asking me
whether or not she's sincere,

00:34:44.912 --> 00:34:47.210
I have to say yes.

00:34:50.451 --> 00:34:52.646
You got to know them very well?

00:34:52.687 --> 00:34:54.314
That's an understatement.

00:34:54.355 --> 00:34:57.324
I heard their thoughts,
felt their feelings,

00:34:57.358 --> 00:35:00.020
saw through their eyes.

00:35:03.364 --> 00:35:05.332
And, in all the time
you were linked,

00:35:05.366 --> 00:35:07.334
you never sensed
anything negative...

00:35:07.368 --> 00:35:09.802
no hidden agenda,
no destructive intent?

00:35:09.837 --> 00:35:12.499
No.

00:35:12.540 --> 00:35:14.838
Bottom line:

00:35:14.875 --> 00:35:17.867
Do you think we should do
what they're asking?

00:35:22.049 --> 00:35:26.679
I really care about what happens
to these people.

00:35:26.721 --> 00:35:31.522
So, in my heart, I'd like to do
everything we can to help them.

00:35:31.559 --> 00:35:34.528
But, if I were sitting
in your chair,

00:35:34.562 --> 00:35:37.827
I'd have to take other
considerations into account.

00:35:42.503 --> 00:35:44.164
Not only would it mean
imposing a choice

00:35:44.205 --> 00:35:47.766
on thousands of people who had
no voice in the decision,

00:35:47.808 --> 00:35:50.538
but it would also be taking
a terrible risk.

00:35:50.578 --> 00:35:53.445
Helping to create
a new collective?

00:35:53.481 --> 00:35:56.678
Who knows what
the repercussions might be?

00:36:02.356 --> 00:36:04.347
I'll let Riley know.

00:36:14.702 --> 00:36:16.932
I'm afraid
her decision was final.

00:36:17.038 --> 00:36:19.666
I wish it weren't,
but I expected as much.

00:36:19.707 --> 00:36:21.334
What about the raiders?

00:36:21.375 --> 00:36:24.173
How long do you think you
can hold out against them?

00:36:24.211 --> 00:36:26.509
Well, we'll just have to do
the best we can.

00:36:26.547 --> 00:36:29.380
Who knows, maybe we'll find some
other way to get to the cube

00:36:29.417 --> 00:36:31.044
and reinitiate the link.

00:36:31.085 --> 00:36:32.143
Come with us.

00:36:32.186 --> 00:36:33.710
Chakotay...

00:36:33.754 --> 00:36:35.415
We could replicate
some Texas barbecue.

00:36:35.456 --> 00:36:36.946
I'm sure it won't
compare to your mother's,

00:36:36.991 --> 00:36:37.958
but I think it...

00:36:37.992 --> 00:36:39.687
Don't think it's not tempting.

00:36:39.727 --> 00:36:41.695
But my place is here.

00:36:41.729 --> 00:36:44.527
I know you understand.

00:36:44.565 --> 00:36:48.433
I've never understood
anyone better in my life.

00:36:50.271 --> 00:36:52.899
Well, we're finished
laying in the supplies.

00:36:52.940 --> 00:36:54.999
Thank you, Neelix.

00:36:56.677 --> 00:36:58.668
Uh, we'd better get going.

00:37:20.368 --> 00:37:21.699
You okay?

00:37:27.441 --> 00:37:30.535
What you need is a good
thrashing on the hoverball court

00:37:30.578 --> 00:37:32.045
to take your mind off things.

00:37:33.546 --> 00:37:35.537
You're on.

00:37:35.581 --> 00:37:37.947
Good. I'll reserve
some holodeck time

00:37:38.051 --> 00:37:39.780
as soon as we're back.

00:37:39.819 --> 00:37:42.879
Chakotay, can you hear us?

00:37:45.558 --> 00:37:47.856
Did you say something?

00:37:47.894 --> 00:37:49.452
No.

00:37:49.495 --> 00:37:52.123
Are you getting
a com transmission?

00:37:52.165 --> 00:37:54.065
No. Why?

00:37:56.002 --> 00:37:59.130
Must've been my imagination.

00:37:59.172 --> 00:38:01.163
You sure you're okay?

00:38:02.675 --> 00:38:04.506
I'm fine.

00:38:06.846 --> 00:38:11.146
Chakotay, we need your help.

00:38:11.184 --> 00:38:12.412
Chakotay?

00:38:12.452 --> 00:38:14.920
We need your help.

00:38:15.021 --> 00:38:16.488
I'm going to tell the Doctor

00:38:16.522 --> 00:38:19.150
he needs to take a look at you
as soon as we're back.

00:38:19.192 --> 00:38:20.420
Torres to Sick Bay.

00:38:20.460 --> 00:38:22.018
Don't do that.

00:38:23.362 --> 00:38:25.353
Chakotay, give me the phaser.

00:38:39.112 --> 00:38:40.579
Captain,
Commander Chakotay's shuttle

00:38:40.613 --> 00:38:41.580
has changed course.

00:38:41.614 --> 00:38:42.979
Try hailing them.

00:38:44.250 --> 00:38:45.274
No response.

00:38:45.318 --> 00:38:47.786
They are increasing speed
to maximum impulse.

00:38:47.820 --> 00:38:49.811
Tom, lay in a pursuit course.

00:38:49.856 --> 00:38:53.451
Tell Neelix we'll rendezvous
with his shuttle later.

00:39:00.233 --> 00:39:06.069
Chakotay,
transport to module 47 omega.

00:39:06.105 --> 00:39:07.902
The bunker is under attack.

00:39:07.974 --> 00:39:09.908
47 omega.

00:39:09.976 --> 00:39:12.240
Section nine, mark coordinates.

00:39:12.278 --> 00:39:13.802
We are under attack.

00:39:13.846 --> 00:39:15.609
Nine alpha alpha.

00:39:15.648 --> 00:39:17.013
We must hurry.

00:39:17.049 --> 00:39:18.676
The bunker is under attack.

00:39:18.718 --> 00:39:20.276
47 omega.

00:39:20.319 --> 00:39:21.616
Section 9.

00:39:21.654 --> 00:39:22.621
Mark coordinates.

00:39:22.655 --> 00:39:24.452
We are under attack.

00:39:34.500 --> 00:39:38.300
Proceed to interlink console
three beta six.

00:39:38.337 --> 00:39:39.861
Hear our thoughts.

00:39:39.906 --> 00:39:41.305
Our thoughts are one.

00:39:41.340 --> 00:39:43.331
Interlink three beta six.

00:39:43.376 --> 00:39:46.743
Proceed to interlink console
three beta six.

00:39:46.779 --> 00:39:48.041
Hear our thoughts.

00:40:08.000 --> 00:40:09.991
Check that area out.

00:40:16.309 --> 00:40:18.300
This way.

00:40:31.224 --> 00:40:35.923
Lower right panel,
attach power conduit 166.

00:40:35.962 --> 00:40:36.929
Hurry.

00:40:36.963 --> 00:40:38.260
Pathway pi two.

00:40:38.297 --> 00:40:40.322
We are under attack.

00:40:40.366 --> 00:40:41.958
Pathway pi two.

00:40:52.378 --> 00:40:55.245
Activate
the neuroelectric generator.

00:40:55.281 --> 00:40:56.339
Quickly.

00:40:56.382 --> 00:40:58.009
Power circuit mechanism.

00:40:58.117 --> 00:40:59.675
Activate the generator.

00:40:59.719 --> 00:41:00.879
Help us.

00:41:00.920 --> 00:41:04.185
We must activate the
neuroelectric generator now.

00:41:04.223 --> 00:41:06.214
Chakotay, need your help.

00:41:06.259 --> 00:41:07.749
Losing time.

00:41:07.793 --> 00:41:11.923
Commander, take your hand
away from that console

00:41:11.964 --> 00:41:13.795
or I will be forced to fire.

00:41:13.899 --> 00:41:16.163
You must not let them stop you.

00:41:16.202 --> 00:41:17.965
You must do this.

00:41:23.342 --> 00:41:25.902
You must move power circuit
mechanism alpha

00:41:25.945 --> 00:41:27.537
to position one.

00:41:38.357 --> 00:41:40.086
Hear our voices.

00:41:40.126 --> 00:41:42.686
We welcome you
into our thoughts.

00:41:42.728 --> 00:41:45.094
Feel the connection.

00:42:04.750 --> 00:42:06.377
Mr. Kim.

00:42:13.192 --> 00:42:14.921
Voyager, emergency beam-out.

00:42:19.932 --> 00:42:22.924
Chakotay, B'Elanna
and the away team are all back,

00:42:22.968 --> 00:42:25.095
and we've tractored in
the shuttle.

00:42:25.137 --> 00:42:27.435
Take us out of here slowly.

00:42:29.809 --> 00:42:31.777
Captain, the Borg ship
is powering weapons.

00:42:31.811 --> 00:42:33.938
Mr. McKenzie, full power
to the shields.

00:42:33.979 --> 00:42:36.174
Arm all phaser banks
and prepare to fire.

00:42:36.215 --> 00:42:37.773
Captain, the Borg ship

00:42:37.817 --> 00:42:39.978
has initiated
a self-destruct sequence.

00:42:40.019 --> 00:42:41.611
It'll go in three seconds.

00:42:41.654 --> 00:42:42.678
Get us out of here.

00:42:51.030 --> 00:42:51.997
Report.

00:42:52.064 --> 00:42:53.691
Shields are holding.

00:42:53.733 --> 00:42:56.429
No injuries or hull damage.

00:42:56.469 --> 00:42:57.993
What the hell
happened back there?

00:42:58.037 --> 00:42:59.937
Audio transmission, Captain.

00:42:59.972 --> 00:43:01.439
From the planet's surface.

00:43:01.474 --> 00:43:03.203
Let's hear it.

00:43:04.577 --> 00:43:06.670
We are the new cooperative.

00:43:06.712 --> 00:43:09.681
We have destroyed the Borg cube.

00:43:09.715 --> 00:43:13.776
We regret that we forced
Commander Chakotay to assist us,

00:43:13.819 --> 00:43:16.720
but it was necessary
for our survival.

00:43:16.756 --> 00:43:20.954
His link with the cooperative
has now been severed.

00:43:21.026 --> 00:43:23.085
Our lasting gratitude.

00:43:31.203 --> 00:43:33.569
His neuropeptide levels
have returned to normal.

00:43:33.606 --> 00:43:35.471
And there are no
residual traces of the link?

00:43:35.508 --> 00:43:36.634
None.

00:43:36.675 --> 00:43:38.540
How were they able
to reestablish the connection?

00:43:38.577 --> 00:43:41.068
My best guess is that
the residual neuropeptides

00:43:41.113 --> 00:43:43.172
heightened
his telepathic receptivity.

00:43:43.215 --> 00:43:45.342
I thought their limited
equipment made it impossible

00:43:45.384 --> 00:43:48.353
for them to form the link
over great distances.

00:43:48.387 --> 00:43:50.981
Apparently, once they repaired
their communications array,

00:43:51.056 --> 00:43:52.990
they were able to use it
to amplify the signal

00:43:53.092 --> 00:43:54.753
from their neural transponder.

00:43:54.794 --> 00:43:56.455
Would you two please excuse us?

00:44:04.270 --> 00:44:08.229
I don't know what to say,
except... I'm sorry.

00:44:08.274 --> 00:44:09.741
Based on what
the Doctor's told us,

00:44:09.775 --> 00:44:12.266
it's clear you were acting
against your will.

00:44:12.311 --> 00:44:13.642
Maybe so.

00:44:13.679 --> 00:44:16.671
But somehow that doesn't
make me feel any better.

00:44:16.715 --> 00:44:19.946
I helped them repair
their communications array,

00:44:19.985 --> 00:44:22.112
and I told you
they were sincere.

00:44:22.154 --> 00:44:25.089
Helping others, Chakotay,
that's part of who you are.

00:44:25.124 --> 00:44:26.819
Given everything you believe in,

00:44:26.859 --> 00:44:29.726
I don't see how you could've
behaved differently.

00:44:29.762 --> 00:44:32.356
But I couldn't have been more
wrong about them, could I?

00:44:33.632 --> 00:44:35.156
I don't know.

00:44:35.201 --> 00:44:38.261
I'm not saying I'm happy
about what happened.

00:44:38.304 --> 00:44:41.637
But, so far, they haven't acted
like typical Borg.

00:44:41.674 --> 00:44:43.574
They saved us from that cube,

00:44:43.609 --> 00:44:45.076
and they let you go.

00:44:45.110 --> 00:44:46.338
But they didn't hesitate

00:44:46.378 --> 00:44:47.970
to impose
their collective will on me

00:44:48.013 --> 00:44:50.243
when it served their interests,
did they?

00:44:50.282 --> 00:44:52.273
No, they didn't.

00:44:52.318 --> 00:44:54.878
I wonder how long
their ideals will last

00:44:54.920 --> 00:44:57.115
in the face
of that kind of power?
